*.DS_Store

# Downloaded tools (not checked in -- own licenses, sizable):
# the Maude binary + prelude, and the Maude Formal Environment (CRC/ChC/MTT).
# See spectec/tools/mfe/README.md for how to obtain them.
spectec/tools/maude/
spectec/tools/mfe/src/
spectec/tools/mfe/examples/
spectec/tools/mfe/license.txt
spectec/tools/mfe/readme.md
# Termination backend (obtained on demand; see spectec/tools/mfe/README.md):
# the hook-enabled Maude 2.7.1 + old MFE 2.7.1 (bundles MTT 1.5j), the AProVE
# jar + its runner, and the maude/MTT scratch files they write.
spectec/tools/maude271-hooks/
spectec/tools/mfe271/
spectec/tools/aprove/
spectec/tools/yices/
spectec/tools/yices1/
spectec/tools/z3/
spectec/log.txt
spectec/term_sweep.tsv
spectec/.hook-check

# check_diff_p4.sh differential-run outputs (per-run verdicts, gap tables, log).
# The harness (check_diff_p4.sh) and reference suite (p4_typecheck_suite.txt)
# stay tracked; only the generated result files are ignored.
/check_diff_p4_*

# check_diff_structural_p4.sh (structural-backend differential) outputs: run
# logs and the PASS&OK shard list. The harness itself stays tracked; the result
# TSVs it writes are already covered by /check_diff_p4_* above.
/check_diff_structural_*.log
/pass_ok.txt

# Personal research notes (not part of the spec/docs; see todo.md/CORE_LOGIC.md
# for the tracked design docs).
/RESEARCH_NOTES.md
